======================================================================
12. EARTH, MARS, LUNAR, AND MICROGRAVITY INTERPRETATION
======================================================================

The predefined gravity conditions permit interpretation of:

1.00 g:
Earth reference

0.38 g:
Mars-equivalent condition

0.16 g:
Moon-equivalent condition

0.00 g:
Microgravity computational condition

The 0.75 g and 0.50 g conditions provide intermediate points for
characterizing the response trajectory.

The intermediate conditions must not be removed from the computational
experiment merely because they are not associated with a specific
planetary environment.


======================================================================
13. GRAVITY-RESPONSE TREND ANALYSIS
======================================================================

The principal scientific interpretation should focus on the direction
and magnitude of mechanical response across decreasing gravity.

The analysis should determine whether decreasing gravity is associated
with changes in:

- myocardial stress;
- myocardial strain;
- ventricular displacement;
- LV cavity volume;
- myocardial volume;
- strain energy.

Any statement regarding monotonicity must be supported by the actual
patient-level numerical outputs.

If a variable does not change monotonically, the manuscript must report
the observed pattern rather than impose a monotonic interpretation.


======================================================================
14. ROBUSTNESS / SENSITIVITY EXPERIMENTS
======================================================================

Sensitivity analyses are separate from the primary gravity sweep.

The primary gravity experiment must use the locked baseline model
configuration.

Sensitivity analyses may subsequently vary predefined assumptions
according to the corresponding sensitivity-analysis design.

The recovered supplementary structure identifies:

- fiber-orientation sensitivity;
- material-parameter sensitivity;
- basal boundary-condition sensitivity;
- cavity-pressure sensitivity.

These analyses should determine whether the qualitative gravity-response
conclusions remain stable under reasonable changes in model assumptions.


======================================================================
15. BASELINE MODEL REQUIREMENT
======================================================================

The baseline gravity experiment must use one locked computational
configuration.

The following should remain fixed across the primary gravity sweep
unless explicitly defined as gravity-dependent:

- patient-specific geometry;
- mesh;
- fiber-orientation mapping;
- constitutive formulation;
- material parameters;
- cavity-pressure specification;
- basal mechanical constraints;
- solver configuration;
- convergence criteria;
- post-processing definitions.

Any deviation must be recorded in the simulation-execution registry.


======================================================================
16. MESH AND NUMERICAL CONFIGURATION
======================================================================

The final mesh selected through the predefined mesh-convergence procedure
must be used for the primary gravity-response experiment.

Mesh selection must precede the final gravity comparison.

A gravity condition should not use a different mesh solely because that
condition produces a different result.

Any gravity-specific remeshing must be explicitly documented and treated
as a separate computational condition.


======================================================================
17. SOLVER AND CONVERGENCE REQUIREMENTS
======================================================================

Each patient-gravity simulation must satisfy the predefined numerical
convergence criteria documented in the COMSOL model and verification
registry.

For every executed simulation, the execution record should retain, where
available:

- solver status;
- nonlinear convergence status;
- residual;
- iteration information;
- failed-element information;
- relevant numerical warnings;
- final exported endpoint values.

A simulation that does not satisfy the predefined convergence criteria
must not be silently included as a successful final simulation.


======================================================================
18. EXECUTION STATUS CLASSIFICATION
======================================================================

Every patient × gravity combination must be classified using the
following evidence categories:

PLANNED
The combination belongs to the predefined experimental design.

EXECUTED
A corresponding computational run was actually performed and an
execution artifact exists.

VERIFIED
The execution passed the predefined numerical/quality-control criteria.

MANUSCRIPT-REPORTABLE
The result is traceable from patient input through execution and
verification to a machine-readable numerical output.

A planned simulation is not automatically executed.

An executed simulation is not automatically verified.

A verified simulation is not automatically manuscript-reportable unless
the numerical result can be traced to the underlying output artifact.


